            "alt": "A toddler cheers as a butterfly flutters up from a leaf."
          }
        },
        "cap": "A toddler cheers as a butterfly flutters up from a leaf."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>gen</b> = <b>birth, kind, produce</b>. <b>morph</b> = <b>form, shape</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "<i>gen</i> hides in words that look nothing alike: <b>genesis</b> (a birth, a beginning), <b>congenital</b> (present from birth), <b>engender</b> (to give birth to, cause), <b>ingenious</b> (clever, as if born with talent) and <b>ingenuous</b> (innocent, as if freshly born)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "gen",
            "morph"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "gen (birth, kind) and morph (shape)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>genesis</b><br>the origin or coming into being",
            "<b>gen</b> <i>birth</i> + -esis<br>→ “a birth (a beginning)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>congenital</b><br>present from birth",
            "con- <i>with</i> + <b>genit</b> <i>born</i> + -al<br>→ “born with”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>engender</b><br>to cause or give rise to",
            "en- <i>in</i> + <b>gender</b> <i>beget, produce</i><br>→ “bring into being”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>ingenious</b><br>clever and inventive",
            "in- <i>in</i> + <b>geni</b> <i>inborn talent</i> + -ous<br>→ “full of inborn talent”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>ingenuous</b><br>innocent and trusting; frank",
            "in- <i>in</i> + <b>genu</b> <i>born</i> + -ous<br>→ “freeborn, open and innocent”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>anthropomorphic</b><br>giving human form or traits to animals or things",
            "anthrop <i>human being</i> + <b>morph</b> <i>shape</i> + -ic<br>→ “in human shape”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>metamorphosis</i></b><br>a complete change of form",
            "meta <i>change</i> + <b>morph</b> <i>shape</i> + -osis<br>→ “a change of shape”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>amorphous</i></b><br>having no clear shape",
            "a- <i>without</i> + <b>morph</b> <i>shape</i> + -ous<br>→ “without shape”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Two look-alikes",
        "q": "Which word fits: (1) “Lila’s ______ plan used a garden hose to water every plant at once.” (2) “The ______ toddler believed every word of the story.”",
        "steps": [
          "Both words have <b>in-</b> + <b>gen</b>, the root of birth.",
          "<b>ingenious</b>: full of inborn talent, so clever and inventive.",
          "<b>ingenuous</b>: as innocent as someone newly born, so trusting and frank."
        ],
        "a": "(1) ingenious; (2) ingenuous."
      },
